n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation."] [:db/add "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)})/(-2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-\\ln(3 x + 2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""] [:db/add "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/answer-fields "9baa3746-90cb-500b-8251-3017a1530a1d"] [:db/add "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/answer-fields "e49426b3-4b2b-5454-8130-574f46902c18"] [:db/add "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/answer-fields "e4198222-2cf0-53fa-a803-9c2fa7bab7c3"] [:db/ensure "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/questions "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc"] [:db/add 